The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
static CLOSURE_CALLBACK(cached_dev_free)
{
    ...
    mutex_unlock(&bch_register_lock);
    // missing: closure_sync(&dc->sb_write);
    if (dc->sb_disk)
        folio_put(virt_to_folio(dc->sb_disk));
    ...
}
```
Reason: The `cached_dev_free` function does not synchronize with an ongoing superblock write (`sb_write`) before deallocating resources. Since `sb_bio` is embedded in the `cached_dev` structure, freeing `dc` (via `kobject_put` later) while the I/O completion callback still references `dc->sb_bio` leads to a use‑after‑free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
+	closure_sync(&dc->sb_write);
+
 	if (dc->sb_disk)
 		folio_put(virt_to_folio(dc->sb_disk));
```
Reason: Adding `closure_sync(&dc->sb_write);` ensures that any pending superblock write I/O has fully completed before proceeding to free the `cached_dev` structure. This prevents the I/O completion callback from accessing the already freed `sb_bio`.

